FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
SOFTWARE.

## 2. Mathematical prose — CC BY 4.0

Applies to `docs/`, `manuscripts/`, `archive/`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and
every other prose document: notes, ledgers, audits, and the manuscript sources
and their compiled PDFs.

Copyright (c) 2026 Lars Bendixen. Licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0). You may share and adapt
this material for any purpose, including commercially, provided you give
appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate whether changes were
made. Full text: <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode>.

Attribution for the mathematics should cite the manuscript and this
repository; see `CITATION.cff`.

## 3. Vendored and imported material

- `mojo/finite_exact/`, `mojo/substitution_dynamics/`, and the other packages
  listed in `vendored.toml` are copied verbatim (up to a recorded import
  rewrite) from `larsbx/finite-math-kernels`, which has the same copyright
  holder. They are covered by section 1, and are re-vendored rather than
  patched; see `AGENTS.md`.
- Imported theorems from the literature are cited, not copied; the citation
  and the audited hypotheses live in the manuscript. No third-party text is
  redistributed here.
